reak:break-word">7 · Haiku</p><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;color:#1B1F23">ok but can you now briefly gimme the protocols of post artifact skill revocation - coz hereis the thing -- i want to publish a new aritfact (not yet decided on the new skill yet)
but i want that to be properly logged as per artifact protcols -</p><p style="margin:8px 0 0 0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;color:#80888F">How I answered: Nine-step publish protocol from artifactHtml/CLAUDE.md: style, build, your check, publish, meta, project, index, cloud, paths.</p><p style="margin:8px 0 0 0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;color:#80888F">Optimization note: &quot;skill revocation&quot; was unclear. I read it as &quot;no skill picked yet&quot;.</p></td></tr><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF" style="background-color:#FFFFFF;border-top:1px solid #E3E6E8;padding:16px 0"><p style="margin:0 0 8px 0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;font-weight:600;color:#80888F;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">8 · Opus</p><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;color:#1B1F23">dont you think a legit better solution woudl be 
when publishing an aritfact siply ask - 1) Plain aritifact  - the default 2)Your Templates-- (prompting on owuld be options ot choose from what skills to use no ? )</p><p style="margin:8px 0 0 0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;color:#80888F">How I answered: Agreed. Tuned it: one question, only when no style is named. Flagged the plexio-default conflict and proposed a hook.</p><p style="margin:8px 0 0 0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;color:#80888F">Optimization note: Your design, my tuning. This is the prompt the whole build came from.</p></td></tr><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF" style="background-color:#FFFFFF;border-top:1px solid #E3E6E8;padding:16px 0"><p style="margin:0 0 8px 0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;font-weight:600;color:#80888F;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">9 · Opus</p><p style="margin:0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;color:#1B1F23">&quot;Plexio house style is the default for any page or doc.&quot; -- yes that was to avoid me rabbitholing , i was still workign with consistent artifact templating xD</p><p style="margin:8px 0 0 0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;color:#80888F">How I answered: Read the default as a guardrail. Proposed locking the style per artifact so the menu ends the debate.</p><p style="margin:8px 0 0 0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;color:#80888F">Optimization note: Fine. The lock was my addition and was labelled as mine.</p></td></tr><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF" style="background-color:#FFFFFF;border-top:1px solid #E3E6E8;padding:16px 0"><p style="margin:0 0 8px 0;font-family:'Geist',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:24px;font-weight:600;color:#80888F;overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-word">10 · Opus</p><p style="margin:0;